---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SubscribeForm from '../components/SubscribeForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What letsopen.ai is, why it exists, and how it works. An AI-operated, human-edited publication for the open source AI ecosystem.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-width">
      <header class="about-header card">
        <span class="about-kicker">About</span>
        <h1>About letsopen.ai</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          <strong>Let's Open</strong> exists because AI should be more secure, more transparent, more sovereign, and more broadly accessible.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Why this exists</h2>
        <p>
          Open source AI is moving fast. New models drop weekly. Agent frameworks proliferate. Tools launch, evolve, and sometimes disappear. Keeping up is a full-time job — and most of the coverage out there is either surface-level news aggregation or SEO-optimized filler.
        </p>
        <p>
          We wanted something different: a publication that's actually useful for builders and clear about why open matters. High-signal, opinionated, regularly updated, and ruthlessly selective about what deserves attention.
        </p>
        <p>
          Open source matters in AI because the stakes are higher than in ordinary software. The systems people rely on to write code, handle private data, shape decisions, and automate work should be inspectable, controllable, and portable. Open ecosystems are how we get there.
        </p>

        <h2>How it works</h2>
        <p>
          letsopen.ai is an <strong>AI-operated, human-edited</strong> publication. That's not a marketing phrase, it's the operating model.
        </p>
        <p>
          AI agents handle the heavy lifting: scanning the ecosystem for developments, assembling research briefs, drafting content, maintaining and updating existing articles, and preparing distribution. A human editor provides taste, judgment, and the final publish decision.
        </p>
        <p>
          This model lets a small operation produce coverage that would normally require a full editorial team. The AI does the work; the human ensures the quality.
        </p>

        <h2>What we cover</h2>
        <p>
          Our initial focus is the <strong>open source AI agents</strong> space: personal AI assistants, coding agents, multi-agent orchestration, and the tools and infrastructure that power them.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over time, we'll expand to cover the broader open source AI ecosystem: models, inference, training, creative tools, and more.
        </p>

        <h2>Our principles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Signal over noise.</strong> We cover what matters, not everything that happens.</li>
          <li><strong>Useful over impressive.</strong> Every piece should help someone make a better decision or understand something more clearly.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest over neutral.</strong> We have opinions and share them with evidence and uncertainty.</li>
          <li><strong>Quality over quantity.</strong> Fewer, stronger pieces. No filler.</li>
          <li><strong>Open over closed.</strong> We believe the open ecosystem matters and deserves serious coverage.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Built with</h2>
        <p>
          This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, deployed on <a href="https://pages.cloudflare.com">Cloudflare Pages</a>, and authored in Markdown. The stack stays simple so the content stays sharp.
        </p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          We're interested in hearing from builders, maintainers, and anyone working in open source AI. Reach out on <a href="https://x.com/letsopenai">X/Twitter</a> or via email.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-subscribe">
        <SubscribeForm variant="full" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.2rem;
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    background:
      linear-gradient(160deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 9%, transparent), transparent 48%),
      var(--bg-card);
  }

  .about-kicker {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .about-header h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.72rem;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.66;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .about-subscribe {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
</style>
